.git
node_modules
strata-qa/node_modules
strata-qa/dist
.logs
.sources
__pycache__
.venv
.pytest_cache

# The image bakes docs/ as the corpus, but runQa only ever reads graph.json,
# INDEX.md, and sources/** (run.ts). Every citation target in graph.json lives
# under sources/, so the audit trail is dead weight in the image — and extra
# search space the retrieval agent can burn tokens wandering into, since the
# corpus root is its cwd. It stays in git; it just does not ship.
docs/.verification
docs/.curation
# Design specs and plans, not corpus: superpowers writes them here and they are
# committed, so this is a real exclusion rather than insurance. They live under
# docs/ for proximity to the work, but the retrieval agent must never search
# them — the corpus root is its cwd, and extra search space is the main cost
# driver. Keeping them out also stops a spec's prose being cited as a source.
docs/superpowers

# Tests never run in the image, and compiling them would put modules that
# `import "vitest"` into dist/ alongside the handler. The fixture modules exist
# only for those tests, so they go too — nothing that ships imports them.
strata-qa/src/**/*.test.ts
strata-qa/src/fixtures.ts
strata-qa/src/lambda/fixtures.ts

# The CLI edge. Nothing the handler can reach imports these — the dependency chain
# runs handler -> lambda/core -> run -> {agent,graph,grounding,log,parse,prompt},
# while cli.ts is a leaf and eval.ts is imported only by cli.ts. Everything the two
# edges genuinely share lives in run.ts by design (see DEFAULT_MODEL there).
#
# Only ~8KB of dist/, so this is about the invariant rather than the bytes: nothing
# ships that the handler cannot reach. fixtures/golden.json is already absent for
# the same reason — the Dockerfile never copies it.
strata-qa/src/cli.ts
strata-qa/src/eval.ts
